  {
    "index": 8,
    "hash": "/vHDaqBCv4BAGpSDNKJLt/bvtk4=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T15:34:49.382Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "A Powerhouse project initialized with `ph init` creates this structure:\n\n- `document-models/` - Document model implementations (schema, gen/, src/reducers, src/tests)\n- `editors/` - React editor components for document types\n- `processors/` - Event-driven components reacting to document changes\n- `subgraphs/` - Modular GraphQL services for structured data access\n\nConfiguration files:\n- `powerhouse.config.json` - Project and Vetra drive configuration\n- `powerhouse.manifest.json` - Package manifest describing contents\n- `package.json` - NPM package metadata (scoped naming: `@org-ph/package-name`)\n- `tsconfig.json` - TypeScript configuration\n- `vitest.config.ts` - Test configuration (the only test/build config scaffolded; see `packages/codegen/src/file-builders/boilerplate/generated-project-files.ts:81`)\n\nThere is **no** `vite.config.ts` in a generated project -- no such template exists under `packages/codegen/src/templates/boilerplate/`. Vite config is supplied by builder-tools and can only be overridden with `ph connect --vite-config-file`.\n\nFor publishing, `powerhouse.manifest.json` declares document models, editors, and their relationships (which editor serves which document type).\n\n_Source-verified 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse source at v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T15:34:44.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T15:34:49.382Z"
    }
  },
